# evpn-vxlan-fabric

Generated by SRL Lab Builder.

## Deploy

```bash
sudo containerlab deploy -t evpn-vxlan-fabric.clab.yml
```

SR Linux image: `ghcr.io/nokia/srlinux:26.7.2`. Log in with `ssh admin@clab-evpn-vxlan-fabric-<node>` (password `NokiaSrl1!`).

## Nodes

| Node | Type | Role | System IP | AS |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| spine1 | 7220 IXR-D3L | spine (RR) | 10.0.0.1 | 65100 |
| spine2 | 7220 IXR-D3L | spine (RR) | 10.0.0.2 | 65100 |
| leaf1 | 7220 IXR-D2L | leaf | 10.0.0.3 | 65001 |
| leaf2 | 7220 IXR-D2L | leaf | 10.0.0.4 | 65002 |
| leaf3 | 7220 IXR-D2L | leaf | 10.0.0.5 | 65003 |
| leaf4 | 7220 IXR-D2L | leaf | 10.0.0.6 | 65004 |
| host1 | linux | host | 172.16.10.1/24 | — |
| host2 | linux | host | 172.16.20.1/24 | — |
| host3 | linux | host | 172.16.10.2/24 | — |

## Check it

```
show network-instance default protocols bgp neighbor
show network-instance default route-table ipv4-unicast summary
show network-instance default protocols bgp routes evpn route-type summary
show network-instance mac-vrf-10 bridge-table mac-table all
show network-instance mac-vrf-20 bridge-table mac-table all
show network-instance tenant-a route-table
show system network-instance ethernet-segments
show lag
```

From a host:

```bash
docker exec -it clab-evpn-vxlan-fabric-host1 ping -c 3 172.16.10.2
```
